# Caddy in front of ket's relay: TLS for relay.ketapp.dev, with certificates
# Caddy gets and renews itself, and WebSockets passed through to the relay on
# loopback. Caddy writes X-Forwarded-For with the client's address, which the
# relay counts sockets against (it trusts the header from loopback alone).
# Install as /etc/caddy/Caddyfile.

# No `log` directive, so Caddy keeps no access log: the relay keeps no record
# of who connected, and nor should anything in front of it.
relay.ketapp.dev {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:7878 {
		health_uri /
		health_port 7879
		health_interval 10s
		health_timeout 2s
	}
}
